WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.210
sum first copies each input to shared scratch storage.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:08.320
A block barrier makes those writes available before partner reads.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:15.840
Each loop stage adds a partner value, and every thread reaches the following barrier, including threads that skipped the addition.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.815
Write shared inputs.

00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:21.370
Each thread supplies its own value.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.675
Synchronise.

00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:25.160
Complete writes before partner reads.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.715
Combine stages.

00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:29.625
Add partners and synchronise before reuse.

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:35.135
Shared memory belongs to the SM and is allocated per resident block.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:41.735
A block barrier orders participating threads; it does not synchronise other blocks on this SM or elsewhere.
